 toward the back, they activate that sensitive bitter zone, making the aftertaste seem localized there. Plus, since you've seen the tongue map, your brain might be hyper-aware of those spots, reinforcing the experience. So your tongue isn't neatly zoned like the old map, but it *is* wired in a way that the tip is great at grabbing sweet signals early, and the back is especially vigilant for bitter threats. That combination makes your personal experience spot-on.
